WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.150
Check yourself with two questions.

2
00:00:02.150 --> 00:00:05.850
First: how does the program
join an IAM role to its record?

3
00:00:05.850 --> 00:00:11.117
The answer is b: four tags, system I
D, owner one, owner two and sponsor,

4
00:00:11.117 --> 00:00:16.188
with one key per owner, because an
AWS tag value can't hold a comma.

5
00:00:16.188 --> 00:00:19.925
Second: the AWS export has no tags file.

6
00:00:19.925 --> 00:00:21.200
What does the kit do?

7
00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:24.557
The answer is b: it runs,
lists the file as not read,

8
00:00:24.557 --> 00:00:27.312
and raises one warning for the account.

9
00:00:27.312 --> 00:00:32.837
A missing file is a warning, never a
pass, and the kit never calls AWS itself.

10
00:00:32.837 --> 00:00:34.956
The module page has three more questions,

11
00:00:34.956 --> 00:00:37.150
each linked to the
section that answers it.
